--- body ---
## Context

The full `make check` after the 0875 identity-split merge fails four existing
country migration tests. `scripts/jetp/_country_migration.py:87`
(`legacy_dispositions`) raises `ValueError: Unclassified country input:
agreements.csv` or `documents.csv` while scanning `data/jetp/`. Both files
already exist on main at `c92e62b9`; neither the 0876 nor 0884 branch adds
them. The temporary country migration readers should distinguish their own
legacy inputs from the ontology-v2 ledger tables introduced by the train.

The separate CRS-data prerequisite is tracked in [[0990]].

## Reproduction and failure map

On `origin/main` `c1e42144`, run `make jetp-data` to materialize pinned JETP
documents, then run the four pytest node IDs below. All four fail in
`legacy_dispositions` at `scripts/jetp/_country_migration.py:87`, before their
country reconciliation assertions run:

| Test node ID (under `tests/`) | Unclassified file |
|---|---|
| `test_jetp_idn_positions.py::test_real_candidate_covers_both_pinned_plan_inventories_and_legacy_rows` | `agreements.csv` |
| `test_jetp_sen_positions.py::test_real_candidate_covers_pinned_inventories_and_keeps_mvp_legacy_owned` | `documents.csv` |
| `test_jetp_vnm_positions.py::test_real_candidate_covers_inventory_legacy_and_all_country_views` | `documents.csv` |
| `test_jetp_zaf_migration.py::test_zaf_candidate_reconciles_inventory_legacy_and_current_views` | `agreements.csv` |

The existing mapping at `_country_migration.py:65-79` lists legacy CSV owners
but has no disposition for these v2 tables. The observed run ended `4 failed
in 42.05s` on main; this is a direct reproduction, not a branch attribution.

## Work

- Inventory every v2 CSV encountered by the scanner, not only the first
  `agreements.csv` or `documents.csv` error in each country. Decide explicitly
  whether each belongs to legacy retained inputs or should be excluded from
  this country migration scan.
- Re-pin country tests that still count pre-0875 `projects.csv` identities;
  keep the legacy-sidecar boundary explicit in a focused test and hand it to
  [[0878]] for migration when compatibility readers are retired.
- Make the scanner apply that disposition without hiding an unknown
  country-specific file. Preserve the country and source-row address.
- Keep the country staging outputs and served views byte-identical.

## Exit criteria

- [x] Four test failures reproduced on main with pinned JETP documents present.
- [x] The four named IDN, SEN, VNM and ZAF pytest nodes pass with v2 tables present (padme, `-n 16`, 2026-09-25).
- [x] An unknown extra input still fails with a named error (`test_ontology_v2_rows_are_excluded_from_legacy_country_dispositions`).
- [x] Country staging outputs and served views are byte-identical before and after (no diff under `data/jetp` or `deliverables/jetp-observatory/data`).
- [ ] `make check-fast` and `make lint` pass; full `make check` passes once [[0990]] supplies its separate CRS data prerequisite.
